@host = http://localhost:5156
@instance = demo
@activity = {{host}}/stateflows/activities/Telemetry/{{instance}}

### Discover the API (Scalar: http://localhost:5156/scalar/v1)
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

### Open SSE in a separate terminal before sending inputs (this request stays open).
GET {{activity}}/output/processedReading?stream=true
Accept: text/event-stream

### Optional second SSE connection for alerts.
GET {{activity}}/output/telemetryAlert?stream=true
Accept: text/event-stream

### Optional third SSE connection for rejected samples.
GET {{activity}}/output/rejectedSample?stream=true
Accept: text/event-stream

### Admit work without waiting for the default 1500ms processing delay: 202 Accepted.
POST {{activity}}/input/sensorSample?sendAsStream=true
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tokens": [
    { "sampleId": "sample-1", "sensorId": "oven", "value": 40, "observedAt": "2026-11-01T20:00:00Z" },
    { "sampleId": "sample-2", "sensorId": "oven", "value": 60, "observedAt": "2026-11-01T20:00:01Z" },
    { "sampleId": "bad-sample", "sensorId": "oven", "value": 20000, "observedAt": "2026-11-01T20:00:02Z" }
  ]
}

### Send within the delay window to steer already admitted work: 40 -> 85, 60 -> 125.
### Otherwise, applies to subsequent batches. This is an ordinary serialized event.
POST {{activity}}/configureTelemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": {
    "gain": 2,
    "offset": 5,
    "alertThreshold": 80,
    "processingDelayMilliseconds": 1500
  }
}

### Ordinary input waits for processing and publishes Transactional output.
POST {{activity}}/input/sensorSample?sendAsStream=false
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tokens": [
    { "sampleId": "ordinary-1", "sensorId": "oven", "value": 40, "observedAt": "2026-11-01T20:00:03Z" }
  ]
}

### A one-shot output watch waits for a FUTURE batch; send input from another connection.
GET {{activity}}/output/processedReading

### Checkpoint waits for active firing bodies to reach the barrier; 200 means committed in memory.
POST {{activity}}/checkpoint

### Status query (may wait behind ordinary processing; not a live progress poll).
GET {{activity}}/status

### Configuration validation: 400, previous configuration is unchanged.
POST {{activity}}/configureTelemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": {
    "gain": 0,
    "offset": 5,
    "alertThreshold": 80,
    "processingDelayMilliseconds": 1500
  }
}

### Empty batches fail admission validation: 400.
POST {{activity}}/input/sensorSample?sendAsStream=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tokens": [] }

### Lengthen the simulated I/O delay to make cancellation easy to observe.
POST {{activity}}/configureTelemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": {
    "gain": 2,
    "offset": 5,
    "alertThreshold": 80,
    "processingDelayMilliseconds": 5000
  }
}

### Admit this, then immediately run the following finalization request.
POST {{activity}}/input/sensorSample?sendAsStream=true
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tokens": [
    { "sampleId": "cancel-me", "sensorId": "oven", "value": 40, "observedAt": "2026-11-01T20:00:04Z" }
  ]
}

### Cancel executing work. Closing an SSE connection does NOT do this.
POST {{activity}}/finalize?mode=Immediate

### Alternative: ordinary queued finalization (use on a separate live instance).
POST {{activity}}/finalize?mode=Queued

### Reset the instance before reusing it; subsequent initialization restores defaults.
DELETE {{activity}}
